From 79ccb14823f3b886bda321a1bc40b28764cdf3e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:13:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fas 4b: Nibe watchdog, settings panel, fuse-current cap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Watchdog timer forces the heat-offset register back to neutral after
  15 minutes with no confirmed pump contact while governor headroom is
  unknown, closing the "no fail-safe on disconnect" gap noted in
  controller.py. New status "watchdog_reset" surfaces this on the
  dashboard status card.
- New Nibe F750 settings card on Settings > System: enable heating
  boost, Lyxläge varmvatten, cheap-hour percentile, and minimum solar
  surplus to boost on — mirrors the EV scheduler's card/state/save
  pattern.
- Fuse Current is now capped at 200A on both the settings form and the
  PATCH /api/settings backend validation, closing the root cause of the
  earlier incident where a voltage (220) was saved as an amperage.

19/19 backend unit tests pass; frontend type-check and lint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9yfcLt9RHbqoZD18y9PT7
